A||||6||rodmcneill||3.4  0-60 Times||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||01-11-2001||01:22 AM||||What would be the approx. 0-60 times of a Fiero GT with the 3.4 Camaro motor installed with no other mods. 5 spd and automatic.||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||01-11-2001||05:59 PM||||That’s easy! With a stock 3.4-liter engine a 2925 lb. fiero (including driver) will go 0-60 mph in 6.54 seconds and run the quarter mile in 14.62 seconds @ 94.2 mph.<P>The same car with the stock 2.8-liter engine runs 0-60 mph in 7.96 seconds and runs the quarter mile in 15.72 seconds @ 86 mph.<P><BR>I got these times using Drapstrip2000.  <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||GarethWright||01-11-2001||06:13 PM||||Any idea on the HP/Torque differences between a 3.4 with fiero parts and a stock 2.8?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero87||01-11-2001||06:13 PM||||Just curious...<BR>Has anyone actually done this and gotton the results above?  If so i have an 87 coupe that could really use such an engine...<BR>Tim||||reg||6
Z||000004||Black88GT||01-11-2001||06:18 PM||||Not sure about those exact times, but I am pretty sure I am somewhere close, click the link and check out why....<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004504.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004504.html</A> <P>The main reason I did the 3.4 was because I needed to get my car running fast and as cheap as possible, without going for the 2.8 again.  The 3.8 takes too long and requires a lot more money.  3.4 is also good if you want to retain the stock look.  However, its got its limitations, and to compete with the bigger engines you will need forced induction of some type...  <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||12
Z||000005||88formula||01-11-2001||09:25 PM||||GarethWright the Differences between the stock motor and the 3.4-liter motor are 140 horsepower (135 for 87-88) for the stock 2.8-liter motor and 165 horsepower for a stock 3.4-liter Camaro motor.<P>The biggest difference between the two is in how much more torque the 3.4-liter engine makes over the stock 2.8-liter engine. Peak numbers don't tell the whole story. With ported heads, higher compression, manifolds, and the GM 12363220 camshaft the 3.4-liter engine makes 185 horsepower. Add headers and you’re over 200. <P>Fiero87 I believe Cliff Pennock (moderator) drove a fiero with a 3.4-liter engine in it. It had the G-tech meter in it also. I don't know what he had for modifications to the engine but I remember reading that he got a 0-60 mph of 6.2 seconds on the G- tech meter. Cliff correct me if I'm wrong.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||3400Fiero||01-12-2001||05:18 PM||||I realize you are asking about the pushrod 3400, but my 88 formula with a 3400DOHC does 0-60 in 5.62 sec, and 1/4 in 14.1 @ 104 mph as measured by the G-tech.  That was also with a marginal clutch.  <P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC<BR>||||reg||1
